response:
 First, notice that whenever cubes are placed, they must either be horizontal or vertical.  The established vertical column at the front must be followed with a horizontal row or vice versa  The solution proceeds with the same logic, and the following picture shows the bottom three layers. [asy]
/* AMC8 2003 #15 Problem */
draw((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,1)--(1,1)--(1,2)--(0,2)--cycle);
draw((0,1)--(1,1)--(1,0));
draw((4,0)--(6,0)--(6,2)--(5,2)--(5,1)--(4,1)--cycle);
draw((5,0)--(5,1)--(6,1));
label(scale(0.8)*"FRONT", (1, 0), S);
label(scale(0.8)*"SIDE", (5,0), S);
label(scale(0.8)*"VERTICAL", (3, 2), N);
[/asy]  Below is the solution with a minimum of three cubes. [asy]
/* AMC8 2003 #15 Problem */
draw((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,1)--(1,1)--(1,2)--(0,2)--cycle);
draw((0,1)--(1,1)--(1,0));
draw((4,0)--(6,0)--(6,2)--(5,2)--(5,1)--(4,1)--cycle);
draw((5,0)--(5,1)--(6,1));
label(scale(0.8)*"FRONT", (1, 0), S);
label(scale(0.8)*"SIDE", (5,0), S);
label(scale(0.8)*"VERTICAL", (3, 2), N);
draw((6,2)--(8,2)--(8,3)--(7,3)--(7,2)--(6,2)--cycle, linewidth(1));
draw((7,2)--(7,3)--(8,3)--(8,4)--(7,4)--(7,3)--cycle, linewidth(1));
label(scale(0.8)*"HORIZONTAL", (7.5,2), N);
label(scale(0.8)*"HORIZONTAL", (7.5,3), N);
[/asy] Since at least one cube must be next to both [asy]draw((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,1)--(1,1)--(1,2)--(0,2)--cycle);[/asy] and [asy]draw((0,1)--(1,1)--(1,0));[/asy], the minimum value of $m+n$ is $\boxed{3}$ unanged.
</visual>

