 Michael rolls three fair dice.
Let {eq}P(F)

{/eq} be the probability of getting {eq}1

{/eq} on a fair die, and {eq}P(\bar{F})

{/eq} be the probability of not getting {eq}1

{/eq} on a fair die. Then we have:

{eq}P(F) \times P(F) \times P(F)= \dfrac{1 * 1 * 1 }{6 * 6 * 6}= \dfrac{1 }{216}

{/eq} 

{eq}P(\bar{F}) \times P(F) \times P(F)= \dfrac{5 * 1 * 1 }{6 * 6 * 6}= \dfrac{5 }{216}

{/eq} 

{eq}P(F) \times P(\bar{F}) \times P(F)= \dfrac{1 * 5 * 1 }{6 * 6 * 6}= \dfrac{5 }{216}

{/eq} 

{eq}P(F) \times P(F) \times P(\bar{F})= \dfrac{1 * 1 * 5 }{6 * 6 * 6}= \dfrac{5 }{216}

{/eq} 

{eq}P(\bar{F}) \times P(\bar{F}) \times P(F)= \dfrac{5* 5 * 1 }{6* 6 * 6}= \dfrac{25 }{216}

{/eq} 

{eq}P(\bar{F}) \times P(\bar{F}) \times P(\bar{F})= \dfrac{5* 5 * 5 }{6* 6 * 6}= \dfrac{125 }{216}

{/eq} 

{eq}P(F,F,F)+P(\bar{F},F,F)+P(F,\bar{F},F)+P(F,F,\bar{F}) +P(\bar{F},\bar{F},F)+P(\bar{F},F,\bar{F})+P(F,\bar{F},\bar{F})= \dfrac{1 }{216} + \dfrac{5 }{216} + \dfrac{5 }{216} + \dfrac{5 }{216} + \dfrac{25 }{216} + \dfrac{5 }{216} + \dfrac{125 }{216}=\dfrac{1}{3}

{/eq} 

<answer>Therefore, the answer is: \dfrac{1}{3}

{/eq} 

</answer>

